<h3 id="speakers">Speakers</h3>

<p><strong>Yaoheng (Mack) Yang</strong> — Assistant Professor, Department of Biomedical Engineering, University of Southern California
<em>Acoustic transparency enabling functional ultrasound imaging through mouse and human skulls</em></p>

<p><strong>Dian Li</strong> — Chee C. Tung (1966) PhD Fellow, Department of Mechanical Engineering, MIT
<em>Dexterous hand tracking using wearable wrist ultrasonic imaging</em></p>

<h3 id="details">Details</h3>

<ul>
  <li><strong>When:</strong> Friday, August 14, 2026, 12:00 – 1:00 PM</li>
  <li><strong>Where:</strong> Building 46-3189, MIT</li>
  <li><strong>Host:</strong> Chaoyi Zhang, Postdoctoral Fellow, Guoping Feng Lab</li>
</ul>

<p>Supported by the SQoL Program, MIT School of Science, and the Feng Lab at the McGovern Institute. Thanks to everyone who came out — and to both speakers for two genuinely complementary talks.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="Seminars" /><category term="Seminars" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The seminar I hosted at the McGovern Institute on how ultrasound is reshaping neuroscience]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">10 Questions for NHP Systems Neuroscience Workshop 2025</title><link href="https://chaoyi-z.github.io/blog/2025/nhp-systems-neuroscience-workshop/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="10 Questions for NHP Systems Neuroscience Workshop 2025" /><published>2025-10-23T13:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-10-23T13:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://chaoyi-z.github.io/blog/2025/nhp-systems-neuroscience-workshop</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://chaoyi-z.github.io/blog/2025/nhp-systems-neuroscience-workshop/"><![CDATA[<p>I attended the <a href="https://www.cnbc.cmu.edu/10-questions-for-nhp-systems-neuroscience-workshop-2025/">10 Questions for NHP Systems Neuroscience Workshop 2025</a>, held October 23–25, 2025 at the historic Mellon Institute at Carnegie Mellon University in Pittsburgh, PA.</p>

