<h3 id="speakers">Speakers</h3>

<p><strong>Sai Zhou</strong> — Ph.D. Candidate, Material Science and Engineering Program, University of California, San Diego</p>

<p><strong>Chonghe Wang, Ph.D.</strong> — Co-founder and CTO, Sonologi, Inc. (MIT)
<em>8 Years in Ultrasound Patch Technology — Full body continuous ultrasound imaging</em>
Forbes 30 Under 30 (North America) · Finalist, National Inventors Hall of Fame · 2023 Highly Cited Researcher (Clarivate)</p>

<h3 id="details">Details</h3>

<ul>
  <li><strong>When:</strong> Friday, July 12, 2024, 9:00 – 10:00 PM EDT</li>
  <li><strong>Where:</strong> Zoom</li>
  <li><strong>Organized by:</strong> HMS-CSSA (Chinese Scientists and Scholars Association at Harvard Medical School)</li>
  <li><strong>Host:</strong> Chaoyi Zhang</li>
</ul>

<p>Great to see so much interest in wearable ultrasound technology — thanks to both speakers for sharing their work, and to everyone who joined the call.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="Seminars" /><category term="Seminars" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A symposium I organized and hosted for HMS-CSSA on wearable ultrasound for cardiovascular monitoring]]></summary></entry></feed>